@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Compositional interprocedural constant and effect summaries

skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFC
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #495057
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F1F3F5
  BorderColor #495057
}

component "CodePropertyGraph\nAST · DFG · resolved calls" as CPG #DBE4FF
component "call_graph_sccs\nvalidated condensation" as SCC #C3FAE8
component "direct evidence\nglobal/parameter/field\nthrow · await · yield" as DIRECT #FFF3BF
component "callee-first solver\nacyclic once · recursive fixed point" as SOLVER #D3F9D8
component "place substitution\nParam(i) through argument i" as SUBSTITUTE #E5DBFF
component "return dependence\nAST + def-use + callee mask" as DEP #FFD8A8
component "checked scalar fold\nliteral · unary · binary · callee" as CONST #C5F6FA
component "product join" as JOIN #FCC2D7
component "EffectAnalysis\nordered summaries · caps · issues" as OUTPUT #C3FAE8
component "conservative widening\nall parameter bits · overdefined" as WIDEN #FFE3E3

CPG --> DIRECT
CPG --> DEP
CPG --> CONST
SCC --> SOLVER
DIRECT --> SOLVER : local candidate
SOLVER --> SUBSTITUTE : current callee summary
SUBSTITUTE --> JOIN : mapped reads/writes
DEP --> JOIN : <latex>M_f = M_f \lor \sigma_s(M_g)</latex>
CONST --> JOIN : <latex>C_f = \bigsqcup_r \operatorname{eval}(r)</latex>
JOIN --> SOLVER : monotone summary update
SOLVER --> OUTPUT : fixed point and scheduler evidence
DEP --> WIDEN : work/depth/allocation or dependency cycle
CONST --> WIDEN : work/depth/allocation bound
WIDEN --> OUTPUT : capped function evidence

note bottom of SUBSTITUTE
  A callee parameter write becomes a caller global/field
  write only when the actual argument carries that place.
end note

note bottom of OUTPUT
  The source CPG is read-only.
  Negative claims require is_complete().
end note

note bottom of DEP
  Typed heap continuation frames hold source-depth state.
  Native call depth is constant in both return evaluators.
end note

legend bottom
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#DBE4FF>| represented CPG evidence |
|<#C3FAE8>| validated graph / completed result |
|<#FFF3BF>| direct local effects |
|<#D3F9D8>| deterministic SCC scheduling |
|<#E5DBFF>| interprocedural place remapping |
|<#FFD8A8>| parameter-return dependence |
|<#C5F6FA>| scalar constant evaluation |
|<#FCC2D7>| product lattice join |
|<#FFE3E3>| incomplete conservative widening |
endlegend
@enduml
